nd rightfully so  oblivion basically represents the  nothingness between the death and  rebirth of  everything and so the idea is that  oblivion is incapable of dying depending  on what fan you talk to  some people will say oblivion is second  to the one above all the one above all  of course being the being that created  everything in existence now this begs  the question  if something like the bifrost allows a  person in a universe to travel to a  pocket dimension within that universe  is there something that allows a person  to leave their universe and travel to  another universe and the answer is  yes now there's actually quite a few of  these so you do have things like the  florida everglades  i know it's weird and then you have  things like the crossroads you have  stuff like the imcron crystal and even  the negative zone to a degree when it  comes to these various things they're  depicted in different ways the  crossroads for example is depicted as a  whole host of winding paths that the  florida everglades when you pass into  that nexus of reality you basically get  the same thing the florida everglades  are kind of interesting because they're  guarded by the man thing and so when you  approach the man thing swamp he'll touch  you and if you feel fear  it'll incinerate you if you feel no fear  you'll be allowed to pass when it comes  to something like the emcron crystal  this is quite literally a crystal that  exists  out there in the universe and that every  universe has its own version of the  emcron crystal think of it as something  akin to a hallway of doors now if you  actually enter the imron crystal you'll  actually encounter what's called the  white hot room which is where  only individuals who are perfect hosts  for the phoenix force can actually  reside jean grey was a really good  example of that but these individual  places can be accessed through magical  means  a person who can alter reality can do it  these individuals are basically able to  kind of pass through these different  barriers with the exception of the nexus  of realities and the man thing swamp  anybody can go through there but once  you  access these different places you can go  to different universes now the biggest  issue that you have here is unless  you're somebody who's experienced in  doing it like the fantastic four doctor  strange or something like that you can  get lost  because it's not as though you go into  this hallway of doors within the imran  crystal basically and there's like  numbers that label every single universe  you could literally spend just  infinite amounts of time passing from  one universe to the next and never get  to where you need to be  and if you're not keeping track of where  you've been you'll never get back to  your home universe and so from there you  go into the various multiversal  organizations themselves and again we're  not going to cover all of them here the  video on comics explained we'll run  through a lot of that stuff but to  highlight some of the finer points as  most of you guys know the time keepers  and the time variance authority exist  on a multiversal level the roles that  the timekeepers in the tva play in  mobile comics are basically identical to  the roles of the marvel cinematic  universe  a big difference is that the timekeepers  exist to ensure they actually come into  existence so they're kind of dicks and  they're usually pretty selfish then  you've got things like the starlight  citadel in  other world which is basically kind of a  gateway to other realities and it's  essentially the home to the captain  britain court the captain britain core  is basically a multiversal team so  there's one captain britain in every  single universe that's designed to  protect that universe which is really  kind of a crappy role because the  captain britain core  those guys aren't very powerful but then  you've got organizations like the exiles  which are designed to travel around the  multiverse facing off against various  threats and is actually a team  consisting of various individuals  from different universes you've got the  temporal empire of king the conqueror so  basically whenever king goes back in  time  in marvel comics traveling into the past  is not enough to create an alternate  reality you have to actually do  something and so there are stories where  kane the conqueror has fought against  the avengers what this does  is it splits off a litany of alternate  realities where he defeated all of the  avengers he defeated only half the  avengers he defeated one avenger and  then was defeated by the rest now  there's all kinds of different universes  based on that and so the temporal  empire of kang is not really a temporal  empire ruled by one particular person  it's a giant multiversal empire ruled by  virtually every version of kang that's  out there and they're largely referred  to as the council of kings and then  you've got places like  limbo which is where a mortise resides  and so on and so forth but the  multiverse is a pretty complex place and  there's a lot that goes on there in the  realm of marvel comics so again  if you guys want to learn more about  this stuff with regards to the  multiverse and marvel comics  make sure you check out the video in the  description which will link you to  comments explained  which will run over all that stuff and  make it easier for you guys to grasp but  with that being said  thank you guys for watching and i will  catch you all later  peace

